#. Translators: name of the add-on, used as the submenu label and the input gestures category.
#. Translators: title of the add-on panel in NVDA's settings.
#. Translators: category of the add-on commands in the Input gestures dialog.
#. Add-on summary/title, usually the user visible name of the add-on
#. Translators: Summary/title for this add-on
#. to be shown on installation and add-on information found in add-on store
msgid "MiSudokuAccesible"
msgstr "MiSudokuAccesible"

#. Translators: item of the add-on submenu that starts a new sudoku.
#. Translators: item of the menu of the sudoku board.
msgid "&New sudoku..."
msgstr "&Nuevo sudoku..."

#. Translators: help text of the "New sudoku" menu item.
msgid "Choose a level and start a new sudoku"
msgstr "Elegir un nivel y empezar un sudoku nuevo"

#. Translators: item of the add-on submenu that opens the sudoku of the day.
msgid "Sudoku of the &day"
msgstr "Sudoku del &día"

#. Translators: help text of the "Sudoku of the day" menu item.
msgid "A new sudoku every day, the same for everyone"
msgstr "Un sudoku nuevo cada día, el mismo para todos"

#. Translators: item of the add-on submenu that opens the sudoku course.
msgid "&Learn to play..."
msgstr "&Aprender a jugar..."

#. Translators: help text of the "Learn to play" menu item.
msgid "Guided lessons to learn sudoku step by step"
msgstr "Lecciones guiadas para aprender sudoku paso a paso"

#. Translators: item of the add-on submenu that shows the statistics.
msgid "My &statistics..."
msgstr "Mis &estadísticas..."

#. Translators: help text of the "My statistics" menu item.
msgid "Sudokus solved, best times, days in a row and your progress in the course"
msgstr "Sudokus resueltos, mejores tiempos, días seguidos y tu progreso en el curso"

#. Translators: item of the add-on submenu that shows all the keyboard shortcuts.
msgid "&Keyboard shortcuts..."
msgstr "Atajos de &teclado..."

#. Translators: help text of the "Keyboard shortcuts" menu item.
msgid "The keys of the board and of the lessons"
msgstr "Las teclas del tablero y de las lecciones"

#. Translators: item of the add-on submenu that opens the sudoku in progress.
msgid "&Continue the sudoku"
msgstr "&Continuar el sudoku"

#. Translators: help text of the "Continue the sudoku" menu item.
msgid "Open the sudoku you left unfinished"
msgstr "Abrir el sudoku que dejaste sin terminar"

#. Translators: label of the add-on submenu inside NVDA's Tools menu.
msgid "Mi&SudokuAccesible"
msgstr "Mi&SudokuAccesible"

#. Translators: help text of the add-on submenu.
msgid "Accessible sudoku"
msgstr "Sudoku accesible"

#. Translators: description of the command that opens the sudoku course, shown in the Input gestures dialog.
msgid "Opens the sudoku course Learn to play"
msgstr "Abre el curso de sudoku Aprender a jugar"

#. Translators: reported when asking for a new sudoku while another one is being prepared.
msgid "A sudoku is already being prepared."
msgstr "Ya se está preparando un sudoku."

#. Translators: asked when starting a new sudoku while another one is unfinished.
msgid "You have an unfinished sudoku. If you start a new one, it will be lost. Start a new sudoku?"
msgstr "Tienes un sudoku sin terminar. Si empiezas otro, se perderá. ¿Empezar un sudoku nuevo?"

#. Translators: title of the confirmation to start a new sudoku.
#. Translators: title of the new sudoku dialog.
msgid "New sudoku"
msgstr "Nuevo sudoku"

#. Translators: said while a new sudoku is generated (it can take a couple of seconds).
msgid "Preparing the sudoku..."
msgstr "Preparando el sudoku..."

#. Translators: reported when a new sudoku could not be generated.
msgid "The sudoku could not be prepared. Please try again."
msgstr "No se pudo preparar el sudoku. Inténtalo de nuevo."

#. Translators: reported when the saved sudoku cannot be opened.
msgid "The unfinished sudoku could not be opened. You can start a new one."
msgstr "No se pudo abrir el sudoku sin terminar. Puedes empezar uno nuevo."

#. Translators: title of the message about the saved sudoku.
msgid "Continue the sudoku"
msgstr "Continuar el sudoku"

#. Translators: said after solving a sudoku faster than ever in that size and level.
msgid "It is your best time in this size and level!"
msgstr "¡Es tu mejor tiempo en este tamaño y nivel!"

#. Translators: said when opening the sudoku of the day after solving it, as in "You already solved today's sudoku. You have solved it 3 days in a row. Come back tomorrow for a new one."
msgid "You already solved today's sudoku. {streak} Come back tomorrow for a new one."
msgstr "Ya resolviste el sudoku de hoy. {streak} Vuelve mañana para uno nuevo."

#. Translators: title of the message about the sudoku of the day.
#. Translators: heading of the statistics.
msgid "Sudoku of the day"
msgstr "Sudoku del día"

#. Translators: asked before starting the sudoku of the day.
msgid "How do you want to play today's sudoku?"
msgstr "¿Cómo quieres jugar el sudoku de hoy?"

#. Translators: button to play the sudoku of the day with hints and clash warnings.
msgid "&With help"
msgstr "&Con ayudas"

#. Translators: button to play the sudoku of the day without hints or clash warnings.
msgid "With&out help"
msgstr "&Sin ayudas"

#. Translators: said while the sudoku of the day is generated.
msgid "Preparing the sudoku of the day..."
msgstr "Preparando el sudoku del día..."

#. Translators: description of the command that opens the sudoku of the day, shown in the Input gestures dialog.
msgid "Opens the sudoku of the day"
msgstr "Abre el sudoku del día"

#. Translators: description of the command that shows the statistics, shown in the Input gestures dialog.
msgid "Shows your sudoku statistics"
msgstr "Muestra tus estadísticas de sudoku"

#. Translators: description of the command that opens the sudoku board, shown in the Input gestures dialog.
msgid "Opens the sudoku board: continues the unfinished sudoku or starts a new one"
msgstr "Abre el tablero de sudoku: continúa el sudoku sin terminar o empieza uno nuevo"

#. Translators: joins the last two items of a list of numbers, as in "1, 4 and 7".
#. Translators: joins the places where a number clashes, as in "in the row and in the block".
msgid "{items} and {last}"
msgstr "{items} y {last}"

#. Translators: a sudoku difficulty level.
msgid "Easy"
msgstr "Fácil"

#. Translators: a sudoku difficulty level.
msgid "Medium"
msgstr "Medio"

#. Translators: a sudoku difficulty level.
msgid "Hard"
msgstr "Difícil"

#. Translators: a size of the sudoku board, as in "9 by 9".
msgid "{size} by {size}"
msgstr "{size} por {size}"

#. Translators: said when pressing a number that is too big for the board, as in "In this sudoku the numbers go from 1 to 4."
msgid "In this sudoku the numbers go from 1 to {last}."
msgstr "En este sudoku los números van del 1 al {last}."

#. Translators: reported for a cell without notes.
msgid "no notes"
msgstr "sin notas"

#. Translators: the notes of a cell, as in "notes 1, 4 and 7".
msgid "notes {numbers}"
msgstr "notas {numbers}"

#. Translators: short form of a cell position, as in "R3C5" (row 3, column 5).
msgid "R{row}C{column}"
msgstr "F{row}C{column}"

#. Translators: a cell position at the start of its description, as in "Row 3, column 5".
msgid "Row {row}, column {column}"
msgstr "Fila {row}, columna {column}"

#. Translators: a cell with a number from the puzzle, which cannot be changed, as in "Row 3, column 5: 7, fixed".
msgid "{cell}: {number}, fixed"
msgstr "{cell}: {number}, fija"

#. Translators: a cell with a number written by the player, as in "Row 3, column 5: 7".
msgid "{cell}: {number}"
msgstr "{cell}: {number}"

#. Translators: an empty cell with notes, as in "Row 3, column 5, empty, notes 1, 4 and 7".
msgid "{cell}, empty, {notes}"
msgstr "{cell}, vacía, {notes}"

#. Translators: an empty cell, as in "Row 3, column 5, empty".
msgid "{cell}, empty"
msgstr "{cell}, vacía"

#. Translators: a cell of the sudoku board when moving into another 3 by 3 block.
msgid "{cell}, block {block}"
msgstr "{cell}, bloque {block}"

#. Translators: a row of the sudoku board, at the start of a sentence.
msgid "Row {number}"
msgstr "Fila {number}"

#. Translators: a column of the sudoku board, at the start of a sentence.
msgid "Column {number}"
msgstr "Columna {number}"

#. Translators: a 3 by 3 block of the sudoku board, at the start of a sentence.
msgid "Block {number}"
msgstr "Bloque {number}"

#. Translators: reported when reading a row, column or block without numbers, as in "Row 3: no numbers".
msgid "{group}: no numbers"
msgstr "{group}: sin números"

#. Translators: reported when reading a full row, column or block, as in "Row 3: complete".
msgid "{group}: complete"
msgstr "{group}: completa"

#. Translators: reported when reading a full row, column or block with repeated numbers.
msgid "{group}: has {numbers}; numbers are repeated"
msgstr "{group}: tiene {numbers}; hay números repetidos"

#. Translators: reported when reading a row, column or block, as in "Row 3: has 3, 5 and 7; missing 1, 2, 4, 6, 8 and 9".
msgid "{group}: has {numbers}; missing {missing}"
msgstr "{group}: tiene {numbers}; faltan {missing}"

#. Translators: said when a row of the sudoku gets its 9 numbers.
msgid "Row {number} complete"
msgstr "Fila {number} completa"

#. Translators: said when a column of the sudoku gets its 9 numbers.
msgid "Column {number} complete"
msgstr "Columna {number} completa"

#. Translators: said when a 3 by 3 block of the sudoku gets its 9 numbers.
msgid "Block {number} complete"
msgstr "Bloque {number} completo"

#. Translators: where a written number clashes, as in "clashes with the 5 in the row".
msgid "in the row"
msgstr "de la fila"

#. Translators: where a written number clashes, as in "clashes with the 5 in the column".
msgid "in the column"
msgstr "de la columna"

#. Translators: where a written number clashes, as in "clashes with the 5 in the block".
msgid "in the block"
msgstr "del bloque"

#. Translators: said when a written number is already in its row, column or block.
msgid "{number}, clashes with the {number} {places}"
msgstr "{number}, choca con el {number} {places}"

#. Translators: said when a note is added to a cell.
msgid "note {number} added"
msgstr "nota {number} puesta"

#. Translators: said when a note is removed from a cell.
msgid "note {number} removed"
msgstr "nota {number} quitada"

#. Translators: said when deleting in a cell that is already empty.
msgid "empty"
msgstr "vacía"

#. Translators: said when deleting the notes of a cell.
msgid "notes deleted"
msgstr "notas borradas"

#. Translators: said when deleting a number, as in "7 deleted".
msgid "{number} deleted"
msgstr "{number} borrado"

#. Translators: reported when the sudoku has no empty cells.
msgid "There are no empty cells."
msgstr "No quedan casillas vacías."

#. Translators: how many empty cells the sudoku has.
msgid "{count} empty cell left."
msgid_plural "{count} empty cells left."
msgstr[0] "Falta {count} casilla."
msgstr[1] "Faltan {count} casillas."

#. Translators: result of checking the sudoku when every written number is right.
msgid "Everything you wrote is right."
msgstr "Todo lo que escribiste está bien."

#. Translators: result of checking the sudoku, without saying which cells are wrong.
msgid "{count} cell is wrong."
msgid_plural "{count} cells are wrong."
msgstr[0] "Hay {count} casilla mal."
msgstr[1] "Hay {count} casillas mal."

#. Translators: part of a duration.
msgid "{count} hour"
msgid_plural "{count} hours"
msgstr[0] "{count} hora"
msgstr[1] "{count} horas"

#. Translators: part of a duration.
msgid "{count} minute"
msgid_plural "{count} minutes"
msgstr[0] "{count} minuto"
msgstr[1] "{count} minutos"

#. Translators: part of a duration.
msgid "{count} second"
msgid_plural "{count} seconds"
msgstr[0] "{count} segundo"
msgstr[1] "{count} segundos"

#. Translators: said when the sudoku is solved; the time is only informative.
msgid "Congratulations, you solved the sudoku! Time: {time}."
msgstr "¡Felicidades, resolviste el sudoku! Tiempo: {time}."

#. Translators: a cell inside a sentence, as in "the 7 only fits in the row 3, column 5".
msgid "the row {row}, column {column}"
msgstr "la fila {row}, columna {column}"

#. Translators: a row inside a sentence, as in "Look at the row 3".
msgid "the row {number}"
msgstr "la fila {number}"

#. Translators: a column inside a sentence, as in "Look at the column 3".
msgid "the column {number}"
msgstr "la columna {number}"

#. Translators: a 3 by 3 block inside a sentence, as in "Look at the block 3".
msgid "the block {number}"
msgstr "el bloque {number}"

#. Translators: hint when the board has a wrong number, as in "Before going on, check the row 3, column 5: the 4 is not right."
msgid "Before going on, check {cell}: the {number} is not right."
msgstr "Antes de seguir, revisa {cell}: el {number} no es correcto."

#. Translators: added to the hint about a wrong number when there are more.
msgid "There is {count} more wrong number."
msgid_plural "There are {count} more wrong numbers."
msgstr[0] "Hay {count} número equivocado más."
msgstr[1] "Hay {count} números equivocados más."

#. Translators: hint when none of the techniques works; it tells the number of a cell.
msgid "None of the techniques I know works here, so here is a number: the {number} goes in {cell}."
msgstr "Ninguna de las técnicas que conozco sirve aquí, así que te digo un número: en {cell} va el {number}."

#. Translators: hint when the sudoku is already solved.
msgid "The sudoku is already solved."
msgstr "El sudoku ya está resuelto."

#. Translators: short hint, as in "You can write a number in the row 3, but first you need an intersection in the block 2."
msgid "You can write a number in {target}, but first you need an intersection in {group}."
msgstr "Puedes escribir un número en {target}, pero antes hace falta una intersección en {group}."

#. Translators: short hint, as in "You can write a number in the row 2, but first you need a pair in the column 6."
msgid "You can write a number in {target}, but first you need a pair in {group}."
msgstr "Puedes escribir un número en {target}, pero antes hace falta una pareja en {group}."

#. Translators: short hint, as in "Look at the row 3: only one number is missing."
msgid "Look at {group}: only one number is missing."
msgstr "Mira {group}: solo le falta un número."

#. Translators: short hint, as in "Look at the block 4: there is a number that only fits in one place."
msgid "Look at {group}: there is a number that only fits in one place."
msgstr "Mira {group}: hay un número que solo cabe en un lugar."

#. Translators: short hint, as in "Look at the row 2: there is a cell where only one number fits."
msgid "Look at the row {row}: there is a cell where only one number fits."
msgstr "Mira la fila {row}: hay una casilla donde solo cabe un número."

#. Translators: full hint, an intersection, as in "In the block 1, the 5 can only go in the row 1, column 2 and the row 1, column 3, which are also in the row 1. So in the row 1 there cannot be another 5 outside those cells."
msgid "In {group}, the {number} can only go in {cells}, which are also in {other}. So in {other} there cannot be another {number} outside those cells."
msgstr "En {group}, el {number} solo puede ir en {cells}, que están también en {other}. Así que en {other} no puede haber otro {number} fuera de esas casillas."

#. Translators: full hint, a hidden pair, as in "In the column 6, the 3 and the 8 can only go in the row 2, column 6 and the row 7, column 6. So those two cells cannot have other numbers."
msgid "In {group}, the {first} and the {second} can only go in {cells}. So those two cells cannot have other numbers."
msgstr "En {group}, el {first} y el {second} solo pueden ir en {cells}. Así que esas dos casillas no pueden tener otros números."

#. Translators: full hint, a pair, as in "In the column 6, the row 2, column 6 and the row 7, column 6 only accept the 3 and the 8. So in the column 6 no other cell can have a 3 or an 8."
msgid "In {group}, {cells} only accept the {first} and the {second}. So in {group} no other cell can have a {first} or a {second}."
msgstr "En {group}, {cells} solo admiten el {first} y el {second}. Así que en {group} ninguna otra casilla puede tener un {first} ni un {second}."

#. Translators: full hint, as in "In the row 3 only the 6 is missing: it goes in the row 3, column 4."
msgid "In {group} only the {number} is missing: it goes in {cell}."
msgstr "En {group} solo falta el {number}: va en {cell}."

#. Primero dónde va el número; después, por qué.
#. Translators: start of a full hint with an intersection or a pair, as in "The 8 goes in the row 3, column 7. Why:"
msgid "The {number} goes in {cell}. Why:"
msgstr "El {number} va en {cell}. Por qué:"

#. Translators: full hint after explaining an intersection or a pair, as in "Therefore, in the block 4, the 7 only fits in the row 5, column 2."
msgid "Therefore, in {group}, the {number} only fits in {cell}."
msgstr "Por eso, en {group}, el {number} solo cabe en {cell}."

#. Translators: full hint, as in "In the block 4, the 7 only fits in the row 5, column 2: the other empty cells already have a 7 in their row, column or block."
msgid "In {group}, the {number} only fits in {cell}: the other empty cells already have a {number} in their row, column or block."
msgstr "En {group}, el {number} solo cabe en {cell}: las demás casillas vacías ya tienen un {number} en su fila, su columna o su bloque."

#. Translators: full hint after explaining an intersection or a pair, as in "Therefore, only the 4 fits in the row 2, column 8."
msgid "Therefore, only the {number} fits in {cell}."
msgstr "Por eso, en {cell} solo cabe el {number}."

#. Translators: full hint, as in "Only the 4 fits in the row 2, column 8: the other numbers are already in its row, column or block."
msgid "Only the {number} fits in {cell}: the other numbers are already in its row, column or block."
msgstr "En {cell} solo cabe el {number}: los demás números ya están en su fila, su columna o su bloque."

#. Translators: days in a row solving the sudoku of the day.
msgid "You have solved it {count} day in a row."
msgid_plural "You have solved it {count} days in a row."
msgstr[0] "Llevas {count} día seguido."
msgstr[1] "Llevas {count} días seguidos."

#. Translators: a line of the statistics, as in "9 by 9, Hard: 5 solved, 2 without help. Best time: 20 minutes."
msgid "{size}, {level}: {count} solved, {without} without help. Best time: {time}."
msgid_plural "{size}, {level}: {count} solved, {without} without help. Best time: {time}."
msgstr[0] "{size}, {level}: {count} resuelto, {without} sin ayudas. Mejor tiempo: {time}."
msgstr[1] "{size}, {level}: {count} resueltos, {without} sin ayudas. Mejor tiempo: {time}."

#. Translators: a line of the statistics, as in "9 by 9, Easy: 3 solved. Best time: 12 minutes and 5 seconds."
msgid "{size}, {level}: {count} solved. Best time: {time}."
msgid_plural "{size}, {level}: {count} solved. Best time: {time}."
msgstr[0] "{size}, {level}: {count} resuelto. Mejor tiempo: {time}."
msgstr[1] "{size}, {level}: {count} resueltos. Mejor tiempo: {time}."

#. Translators: statistics when no sudoku has been solved yet.
msgid "You have not solved any sudoku yet."
msgstr "Todavía no has resuelto ningún sudoku."

#. Translators: a line of the statistics about the sudoku of the day.
msgid "Days in a row: {count}."
msgstr "Días seguidos: {count}."

#. Translators: a line of the statistics about the sudoku of the day.
msgid "Record: {count} day in a row."
msgid_plural "Record: {count} days in a row."
msgstr[0] "Récord: {count} día seguido."
msgstr[1] "Récord: {count} días seguidos."

#. Translators: a line of the statistics about the sudoku of the day.
msgid "Solved in total: {count}."
msgstr "Resueltos en total: {count}."

#. Translators: a line of the statistics about the sudoku of the day.
msgid "Today's sudoku is already solved."
msgstr "El sudoku de hoy ya está resuelto."

#. Translators: a line of the statistics about the course.
msgid "Lessons finished: {done} of {total}."
msgstr "Lecciones terminadas: {done} de {total}."

#. Translators: a line of the statistics about the course.
msgid "Stars: {stars} of {total}."
msgstr "Estrellas: {stars} de {total}."

#. Translators: a line of the statistics, as in "Best practice in lesson 4, Last number: 13 of 15."
msgid "Best practice in lesson {id}, {title}: {stars} of {total}."
msgstr "Mejor práctica en la lección {id}, {title}: {stars} de {total}."

#. Translators: heading of the statistics.
msgid "Sudokus solved"
msgstr "Sudokus resueltos"

#. Translators: heading of the statistics.
#. Translators: title of the list of lessons of the course.
msgid "Learn to play"
msgstr "Aprender a jugar"

#. Translators: instruction of an exercise where the whole sudoku is solved.
msgid "Solve the whole sudoku. Press P or Shift+P whenever you need a hint."
msgstr "Resuelve el sudoku entero. Pulsa P o Mayúsculas+P siempre que necesites una pista."

#. Translators: after the instruction of an exercise about a technique.
msgid "Find it and write it."
msgstr "Encuéntralo y escríbelo."

#. Translators: what to do in the first step of an intersection or pair exercise, as in "Remove note 7 from the row 3, column 7."
msgid "Remove note {numbers} from {cell}."
msgid_plural "Remove notes {numbers} from {cell}."
msgstr[0] "Quita la nota {numbers} de {cell}."
msgstr[1] "Quita las notas {numbers} de {cell}."

#. Translators: before the first step of an intersection or pair exercise.
msgid "Step 1 of 2."
msgstr "Paso 1 de 2."

#. Translators: before the second step of an intersection or pair exercise.
msgid "Step 2 of 2."
msgstr "Paso 2 de 2."

#. Translators: second step of an exercise, as in "Now only one note is left in the row 3, column 7. Write that number."
msgid "Now only one note is left in {cell}. Write that number."
msgstr "Ahora en {cell} queda una sola nota. Escribe ese número."

#. Translators: said when writing in another cell in the second step, as in "Not here. Write in the row 3, column 7."
msgid "Write in {cell}."
msgstr "Escribe en {cell}."

#. Translators: short hint of the second step, as in "Press N in the row 3, column 7: only one note is left."
msgid "Press N in {cell}: only one note is left."
msgstr "Pulsa N en {cell}: queda una sola nota."

#. Translators: second step of an exercise, as in "Now, in the row 2, the 1 only fits in one cell. Find it and write it."
msgid "Now, in {group}, the {number} only fits in one cell. Find it and write it."
msgstr "Ahora, en {group}, el {number} solo cabe en una casilla. Encuéntrala y escríbelo."

#. Translators: said when writing in another cell in the second step, as in "In the row 2, the 1 only fits in one cell now."
msgid "In {group}, the {number} only fits in one cell now."
msgstr "Ahora, en {group}, el {number} solo cabe en una casilla."

#. Translators: short hint of the second step, as in "Press N in the empty cells of the row 2: only one still has note 1."
msgid "Press N in the empty cells of {group}: only one still has note {number}."
msgstr "Pulsa N en las casillas vacías de {group}: solo una tiene todavía la nota {number}."

#. Translators: full hint of the second step, as in "The 8 goes in the row 3, column 7."
msgid "The {number} goes in {cell}."
msgstr "El {number} va en {cell}."

#. Translators: short hint of the first step of an intersection or pair exercise.
msgid "Notes are removed with Shift and the number, the same keys that add them. N reads the notes of a cell."
msgstr "Las notas se quitan con Mayúsculas y el número, las mismas teclas que las ponen. N lee las notas de una casilla."

#. Translators: short hint of an exercise, as in "Press B inside the block 4 to hear which number is missing."
msgid "Press {key} inside {group} to hear which number is missing."
msgstr "Pulsa {key} en {group} para saber qué número falta."

#. Translators: short hint of an exercise, as in "Look for the 7: in the block 4 it only fits in one cell."
msgid "Look for the {number}: in {group} it only fits in one cell."
msgstr "Busca el {number}: en {group} solo cabe en una casilla."

#. Translators: short hint of an exercise about a cell where only one number fits.
msgid "Go through the empty cells of the row {row} and press C and B in each one: in one of them only one number fits."
msgstr "Recorre las casillas vacías de la fila {row} y pulsa C y B en cada una: en una de ellas solo cabe un número."

#. Translators: instruction of an exercise about notes, as in "Write as notes in the row 3, column 5 all the numbers that can go there."
msgid "Write as notes in {cell} all the numbers that can go there."
msgstr "Pon como notas en {cell} todos los números que pueden ir."

#. Translators: short hint of an exercise about notes.
msgid "Press F, C and B to hear which numbers are already in its row, its column and its block."
msgstr "Pulsa F, C y B para saber qué números ya están en su fila, su columna y su bloque."

#. Translators: full hint of an exercise about notes, as in "The numbers that can go are 3, 5 and 8."
msgid "The numbers that can go are {numbers}."
msgstr "Los números que pueden ir son: {numbers}."

#. Translators: praise when an exercise of the course is done.
msgid "Very good!"
msgstr "¡Muy bien!"

#. Translators: praise when an exercise of the course is done.
msgid "Excellent!"
msgstr "¡Excelente!"

#. Translators: praise when an exercise of the course is done.
msgid "You did it!"
msgstr "¡Lo lograste!"

#. Translators: praise when an exercise of the course is done.
msgid "Well done!"
msgstr "¡Bien hecho!"

#. Translators: stars earned in an exercise of the course.
msgid "You earned {count} star."
msgid_plural "You earned {count} stars."
msgstr[0] "Ganaste {count} estrella."
msgstr[1] "Ganaste {count} estrellas."

#. Translators: said when trying to change the board of an exercise that is already done.
msgid "This exercise is already done."
msgstr "Este ejercicio ya está hecho."

#. Translators: reported when trying to change a cell with a number from the puzzle.
msgid "fixed"
msgstr "fija"

#. Translators: said when writing a number in an exercise about notes.
msgid "In this exercise you only write notes: press Shift and the number."
msgstr "En este ejercicio solo pones notas: pulsa Mayúsculas y el número."

#. Translators: said when writing a number in an exercise about deleting.
msgid "In this exercise you only delete: press Delete on the wrong number."
msgstr "En este ejercicio solo borras: pulsa Suprimir sobre el número equivocado."

#. En los ejercicios de técnicas no se dice la casilla: encontrarla es el ejercicio.
#. Translators: said when writing in another cell in an exercise about a technique, as in "Not here. Look at the block 4: ..."
msgid "Not here. {orientation}"
msgstr "Aquí no. {orientation}"

#. Translators: said when writing outside the cells of the exercise, as in "In this exercise, write in the row 1, column 4."
msgid "In this exercise, write in {cells}."
msgstr "En este ejercicio, escribe en {cells}."

#. Translators: said when writing or deleting in the step where notes must be removed.
msgid "In this step you only remove notes: press Shift and the number of the note."
msgstr "En este paso solo quitas notas: pulsa Mayúsculas y el número de la nota."

#. Translators: said when a number is already in the row, column or block, as in "The 3 is already in the row 1. Try another one."
msgid "The {number} is already in {group}. Try another one."
msgstr "El {number} ya está en {group}. Prueba con otro."

#. Translators: said when a number does not clash but is not the right one.
msgid "The {number} does not go here. Try another one."
msgstr "El {number} no va aquí. Prueba con otro."

#. Translators: reported when adding a note to a cell that already has a number.
msgid "The cell has a number. Delete it to write notes."
msgstr "La casilla tiene un número. Bórralo para escribir notas."

#. Translators: said when touching another note in the step where notes must be removed, as in "Not that one. Remove note 7 from the row 3, column 7."
msgid "Not that one. {orientation}"
msgstr "Esa no. {orientation}"

#. Translators: said when writing notes outside the cells of the exercise.
msgid "In this exercise, write the notes in {cells}."
msgstr "En este ejercicio, pon las notas en {cells}."

#. Translators: said when a note cannot go in a cell, as in "The 2 cannot go here: it is already in the column 1."
msgid "The {number} cannot go here: it is already in {group}."
msgstr "El {number} no puede ir aquí: ya está en {group}."

#. Translators: said when deleting a right number in an exercise about deleting the wrong ones.
msgid "That number is right. Look for the wrong one."
msgstr "Ese número está bien. Busca el que está mal."

#. Translators: heading in the list of keyboard shortcuts.
msgid "Moving around the board"
msgstr "Moverse por el tablero"

#. Translators: description in the list of keyboard shortcuts.
msgid "Move between the cells"
msgstr "Moverse por las casillas"

#. Translators: description in the list of keyboard shortcuts.
msgid "First or last cell of the row"
